//! `leaked` leaves a file handle open.
//!
//! The source ends with its linear end open. The checker refuses it as
//! `LinearResidue`.
//!
//! The checker settles `File.Handle` against the final residue.
//! The source imports `File` from `file-base`.
//!
//! Rust `std::mem::forget` is safe. It does not run a destructor.
//! - cites: [Rust-std]
//! - see: file-base.gandr — the file protocol
//!
//! [Rust-std]: https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/ "The Rust Project, The Rust Standard Library"
import "../../model/moves/file-base.gandr";

/// `leaked` returns with a handle in its linear slot.
@[ refuses("LinearResidue") ]
def leaked() -> Unit =
  let file = fork (owner : File.Handle) { close owner };
  pure *{}
